{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '1,330p'; rg -n 'identity|higher.order|returned|callback|bag|token|descriptor|cell-ref' test/yang/call\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '1,330p'; rg -n 'identity|higher.order|returned|callback|bag|token|descriptor|cell-ref' test/yang/call\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.call.conformance\n     2\t  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n     3\t   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n     4\t   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n     5\t\n     6\t   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n     7\t   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n     8\t   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n     9\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`, `py/run-main`,\n    10\t   `clj/run-main`), reads each named export from the donor runtime's global\n    11\t   namespace, and projects it into the caller runtime's namespace under the\n    12\t   same name; then the caller source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own\n    13\t   entry. The composition is a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is\n    14\t   rewritten, no foreign `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is\n    15\t   inserted, and the projected value is the donor's own callable value\n    16\t   (identity survives).\n    17\t\n    18\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n    19\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n    20\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n    21\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n    22\t\n    23\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n    24\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n    25\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\n    26\t   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\n    27\t   refused until L-b.\"\n    28\t  (:require\n    29\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    30\t    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\n    31\t    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\n    32\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    33\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\n    34\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    35\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n    36\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n    37\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n    38\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n    39\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\n    40\t    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\n    41\t    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\n    42\t    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\n    43\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n    44\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    45\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n    46\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n    47\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(def ^:private published-php\n    51\t  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n    52\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n    53\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n    54\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n    55\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(def ^:private published-py\n    59\t  \"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\n    60\t   `yang.call` revision.\"\n    61\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n    62\t           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n    63\t                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(def ^:private published-clj\n    67\t  \"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\n    68\t   and `yang.call` revision.\"\n    69\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n    70\t           (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n    71\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn- parse-ok\n    75\t  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n    76\t  [parse source]\n    77\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\n    78\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n    79\t      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n    80\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n    81\t    pk))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t(defn- python-export-symbol\n    85\t  [export]\n    86\t  (symbol (str \"xlang.python.export.\" export)))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- python-unit\n    90\t  [packet exports]\n    91\t  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\n    92\t         (u/seq-nodes\n    93\t           (concat (map (fn [export]\n    94\t                          (u/sexp->uast\n    95\t                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\n    96\t                                  {:py/str export} (python-export-symbol export))))\n    97\t                        exports)\n    98\t                   [(py-lower/lower-module-body packet)]))))\n    99\t\n   100\t\n   101\t(def frontends\n   102\t  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n   103\t\n   104\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n   105\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n   106\t   - `:deps` (optional): pinned requirements beyond the runtime its\n   107\t     lowered units read directly (the clojure unit's `yang.call` reads);\n   108\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n   109\t   - `:unit`: packet and projected exports to the lowered unit its\n   110\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\n   111\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n   112\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table, Python's main\n   113\t     module dictionary, the clojure runtime's task-local namespace cell);\n   114\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n   115\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name;\n   116\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n   117\t  {:typescript\n   118\t   {:runtime 'js,\n   119\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\n   120\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\n   121\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\n   122\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit packet))),\n   123\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\n   124\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\n   125\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\n   126\t    :render render/output},\n   127\t   :php\n   128\t   {:runtime 'php,\n   129\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\n   130\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\n   131\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\n   132\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body packet))),\n   133\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\n   134\t    :read-export (fn [export]\n   135\t                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\n   136\t    :project (fn [name value]\n   137\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n   138\t    :render php-h/render},\n   139\t   :python\n   140\t   {:runtime 'py,\n   141\t    :address #(:address @published-py),\n   142\t    :refusal [:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free],\n   143\t    :parse #(parse-ok py-parser/parse-source %),\n   144\t    :unit python-unit,\n   145\t    :run-main 'py/run-main,\n   146\t    :read-export (fn [export]\n   147\t                   (list 'py/global-get\n   148\t                         (list 'py/module-dict\n   149\t                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \"__main__\"}))\n   150\t                         {:py/str export})),\n   151\t    :project (fn [name value]\n   152\t               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\n   153\t    :render py-render/output},\n   154\t   :clojure\n   155\t   {:runtime 'clj,\n   156\t    :address #(:address @published-clj),\n   157\t    :refusal [:yang.clojure/refusal :yang.clojure/undeclared-free],\n   158\t    :deps (fn [] {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published)}),\n   159\t    :parse clj-comp/read-forms,\n   160\t    :unit (fn [packet exports] (clj-comp/lower-unit packet exports)),\n   161\t    :run-main 'clj/run-main,\n   162\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'clj/global-get export)),\n   163\t    :project (fn [name value]\n   164\t               ;; The runtime global namespace is the one binding (as\n   165\t               ;; `js/define-global!` is for a JS caller): `lower-unit`\n   166\t               ;; reads each projected name through `clj/global-get`, so\n   167\t               ;; no task-store binding duplicates it. A caller top-level\n   168\t               ;; definition of the same name publishes after the\n   169\t               ;; projection and shadows it.\n   170\t               (list 'clj/define-global! name value)),\n   171\t    :render clj-comp/output}})\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\t(defn- profile\n   175\t  [frontend]\n   176\t  (or (get frontends frontend)\n   177\t      (throw (ex-info \"frontend not admitted\" {:frontend frontend}))))\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t(defn- modules\n   181\t  \"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it,\n   182\t   with the clojure guest library's host surface installed beside them.\n   183\t   Donor publication declares free names over this same registry, so a\n   184\t   clojure donor using the guest library (its `kind` and `portable`\n   185\t   hosts) publishes like it runs.\"\n   186\t  []\n   187\t  (clj-prelude/admit (php-prelude/admit (h/registry))))\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t(defn publish-donor!\n   191\t  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n   192\t   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n   193\t   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n   194\t  ([frontend source]\n   195\t   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n   196\t  ([frontend source module]\n   197\t   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\n   198\t         [refusal-key reason] refusal\n   199\t         spec (core-module/module-spec\n   200\t                refusal-key reason (modules)\n   201\t                {:name module,\n   202\t                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\n   203\t                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n   204\t                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))]),\n   205\t                 :exports '#{body},\n   206\t                 :runtime-name runtime,\n   207\t                 :runtime-address (address),\n   208\t                 :deps (if deps (deps) {})})\n   209\t         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n   210\t     {:frontend frontend,\n   211\t      :module module,\n   212\t      :address (:address result),\n   213\t      :links (:links result)})))\n   214\t\n   215\t\n   216\t(defn- runtime-entry\n   217\t  \"Require and initialize each distinct runtime of `frontend-keys`, once.\"\n   218\t  [frontend-keys]\n   219\t  (into [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)]\n   220\t        (mapcat (fn [runtime]\n   221\t                  [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n   222\t                   (u/sexp->uast (list (symbol (str runtime) \"init!\")))]))\n   223\t        (distinct (map (comp :runtime profile) frontend-keys))))\n   224\t\n   225\t\n   226\t(defn- donor-run\n   227\t  \"The donor module required and its body run under its runtime's entry.\"\n   228\t  [{:keys [frontend module]}]\n   229\t  [(core-module/require-node module)\n   230\t   (u/app (u/v (:run-main (profile frontend)))\n   231\t          (u/v (symbol (str module) \"body\")))])\n   232\t\n   233\t\n   234\t(defn export-program\n   235\t  \"The program whose value is the donor's `export`, read from its runtime's\n   236\t   global namespace after its body ran.\"\n   237\t  [donor export]\n   238\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))]\n   239\t    (u/mark-tails\n   240\t      (u/seq-nodes (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor)])\n   241\t                           (donor-run donor)\n   242\t                           [(u/sexp->uast (read-export export))])))))\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn compose\n   246\t  \"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\n   247\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\n   248\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\n   249\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\"\n   250\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n   251\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\n   252\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\n   253\t    (u/mark-tails\n   254\t      (u/seq-nodes\n   255\t        (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor) caller-frontend])\n   256\t                (donor-run donor)\n   257\t                (map (fn [export]\n   258\t                       (let [value (symbol (str \"xlang.export.\" export))]\n   259\t                         (u/let1 value\n   260\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (read-export export))\n   261\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (project export value)))))\n   262\t                     exports)\n   263\t                [(u/app (u/v run-main) (unit (parse caller-source) exports))])))))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn link-source\n   267\t  \"The serving composition naming the runtimes and the donor module.\"\n   268\t  [{:keys [module address]}]\n   269\t  (h/source {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published),\n   270\t             'js (:address @h/published),\n   271\t             'php (:address @published-php),\n   272\t             'py (:address @published-py),\n   273\t             'clj (:address @published-clj),\n   274\t             module address}))\n   275\t\n   276\t\n   277\t(defn run-program\n   278\t  \"`{backend value}` of `ast`, linked against `donor`, on each vector VM.\"\n   279\t  [donor ast]\n   280\t  (let [src (link-source donor)]\n   281\t    (into (sorted-map)\n   282\t          (map (fn [backend]\n   283\t                 [backend\n   284\t                  (vm/value (h/run-linked backend ast {:modules (modules),\n   285\t                                                       :link-source src}))]))\n   286\t          (keys h/backends))))\n   287\t\n   288\t\n   289\t(defn agreed\n   290\t  \"The one value every backend of `results` answered, else\n   291\t   `{:disagreement results}`.\"\n   292\t  [results]\n   293\t  (let [vs (set (vals results))]\n   294\t    (if (= 1 (count vs)) (first vs) {:disagreement results})))\n   295\t\n   296\t\n   297\t(defn call\n   298\t  \"Publish the donor `[frontend source]`, compose its `exports` into the\n   299\t   caller `[frontend source]`, run it on each vector VM and answer the\n   300\t   caller's rendered value when every backend agrees (else\n   301\t   `{:disagreement {backend rendered}}`).\"\n   302\t  [[donor-frontend donor-source] exports [caller-frontend caller-source]]\n   303\t  (let [donor (publish-donor! donor-frontend donor-source)\n   304\t        render (:render (profile caller-frontend))]\n   305\t    (agreed (update-vals (run-program donor (compose donor exports caller-frontend\n   306\t                                                     caller-source))\n   307\t                         render))))\ntest/yang/call/conformance.clj:16:   (identity survives).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
