h reduced)/into/concat/merge,\n  2423\t;; keys/vals/disj and set union/difference,\n  2424\t;; comp, partial, gensym (explicit supply), not=, and `apply`, which is a\n  2425\t;; compiler intrinsic over the convention's argument vector.\n  2426\t;;\n  2427\t;; What stays a host primitive, named by the `kind` module: a symbol, a\n  2428\t;; keyword and a host string are distinguished or built only by the host\n  2429\t;; (symbol?, keyword?, name, symbol, keyword, str, int?), as is metadata access\n  2430\t;; (meta and with-meta). The current data ABI has no metadata-write export,\n  2431\t;; so with-meta is an explicit pure representation seam, not an ambient store.\n  2432\t;; No VM primitive tells a symbol from a keyword. Clojure Var identity is an\n  2433\t;; explicitly admitted kind/var? seam on the JVM; namespace lookup (resolve)\n  2434\t;; still requires a separately installed host capability.\n  2435\t;;\n  2436\t;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\n  2437\t;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\n  2438\t;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\n  2439\t;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\n  2440\t;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\n  2441\t;; When collection calls are needed, invoke-value is a library helper whose\n  2442\t;; local capture is refused explicitly.\n  2443\t;;\n  2444\t;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity here (the convention has no\n  2445\t;; variadic parameter): str, list and vector admit 0 to 6 arguments, concat and\n  2446\t;; merge 0 to 4, union 0 to 6, difference 2, comp 0 to 3, partial binds 1 to 3.\n  2447\t;; A larger count is the\n  2448\t;; function's own arity error.\n  2449\t\n  2450\t(def library-adapters\n  2451\t  \"The `:adapters` a program using `library` is compiled with: the data\n  2452\t   exports whose refusal the predica