ret kind id))\n   351\t                      (= (= :cursor-ref kind) (cursor-cell? resource))))))))\n   352\t\n   353\t\n   354\t(defn check-ref!\n   355\t  \"The resource id a program-supplied `kind` reference names, once its\n   356\t   seal verifies (r10). Anything else fails closed with\n   357\t   `:forged-resource-reference`, naming the effect and the id it named;\n   358\t   a cell ref whose id the heap does not hold is\n   359\t   `:dead-or-forged-reference` instead: its cell was swept, or never was.\n   360\t   Ids are never reused, so such a ref is never silently reallocated.\"\n   361\t  [state effect-kind kind ref]\n   362\t  (if (authentic-ref? state kind ref)\n   363\t    (:id ref)\n   364\t    (let [id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))\n   365\t          dead? (and (= :cell-ref kind) (not (contains? (:heap state) id)))]\n   366\t      (fail (if dead? \"Dead or forged cell reference\" \"Forged resource reference\")\n   367\t            {:reason (if dead?\n   368\t                       :dead-or-forged-reference\n   369\t                       :forged-resource-reference),\n   370\t             :effect effect-kind,\n   371\t             :kind kind,\n   372\t             :id id}))))\n   373\t\n   374\t\n   375\t(declare gensym)\n   376\t\n   377\t\n   378\t(defn attach-resource\n   379\t  \"Install the host stream `handle` a composition hands a task under a\n   380\t   fresh resource id, and return `[stream-ref state]` with the reference\n   381\t   sealed under the task's secret. This is how a stream reaches a program:\n   382\t   never through the store.\"\n   383\t  [state handle]\n   384\t  (let [[id state] (gensym state \"stream\")\n   385\t        ref (issue-ref state :stream-ref id)]\nrg: src/cljc/yin/vm/cell.cljc: IO error for operation on src/cljc/yin/vm/cell.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
