{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'cell/authentic|authentic-ref\\\\?|:cell/get|cell/get' src/cljc/yin/vm/modules* src/cljc/yin/cell* src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3550,3598p;3807,3830p;4017,4033p'; rg -n 'two.API|position.decided|reference position|cell-ref|D2' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.clojure.md docs/design/yang.clojure.md; nl -ba docs/design/datom.world.md | sed -n '7,32p;48,60p;112,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"zsh:1: no matches found: src/cljc/yin/vm/modules*\n  3550\tConstructors and asynchronous operations keep their declared source\n  3551\tsemantics; ordinary callability does not imply either capability.\n  3552\t\n  3553\t#### 8.10.2 Callable representation and identity\n  3554\t\n  3555\tKeep the callable's existing identity and source-specific data. Add the\n  3556\tcommon entry beside its private code and metadata:\n  3557\t\n  3558\t```clojure\n  3559\t;; Illustrative contents of one task-owned Python function cell.\n  3560\t;; `entry` and `body-code` are live Yin closures, not literal AST maps.\n  3561\t{:yang.call/entry entry\n  3562\t :py/type :function\n  3563\t :spec parameter-spec\n  3564\t :defaults defaults\n  3565\t :code body-code}\n  3566\t```\n  3567\t\n  3568\tThe existing `:code` field is not the shared entry: its signature differs\n  3569\tbetween preludes. It may remain private. Cross-language callers must not\n  3570\tinspect it or extract it to bypass the entry.\n  3571\t\n  3572\tA cell-backed callable stores the entry in its cell contents. An\n  3573\timmutable callable descriptor, such as a bound method, may carry it\n  3574\tdirectly in its map. The common prelude projects the entry structurally:\n  3575\tread an existing sealed cell reference through `cell/get`, or inspect\n  3576\tthe immutable descriptor, then obtain `:yang.call/entry`. It must not\n  3577\tdispatch on `:py/type`, `:js/type`, `:php/type`, language names, or a\n  3578\tregistry of languages.\n  3579\t\n  3580\tAn admitted callable is a runtime cell/descriptor constructed or exposed\n  3581\tby the callable constructors or import/export projections of a pinned,\n  3582\tconforming profile. The entry slot is a runtime descriptor field, not a\n  3583\tsource property that promotes arbitrary data to a function. A Python\n  3584\tdictionary, JavaScript object, or PHP array containing a source key\n  3585\tspelled `:yang.call/entry` remains ordinary source data unless an explicit\n  3586\tprofile-defined projection makes it a callable descriptor. Source\n  3587\tproperty access must not overwrite or masquerade as this runtime slot.\n  3588\tThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\n  3589\tVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\n  3590\tthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\n  3591\tUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\n  3592\tconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n  3593\t\n  3594\tMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\n  3595\tunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\n  3596\tinvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\n  3597\tnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\n  3598\tVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\n  3807\t#### 8.10.6 References, higher-order calls, and ownership\n  3808\t\n  3809\tBy-value arguments may contain shared object references. That does not\n  3810\tauthorize rebinding the caller's variable: a value read from a local is\n  3811\tnot a location capability.\n  3812\t\n  3813\tSource-local reference arguments keep their pinned native binding\n  3814\tprofile. A call requiring foreign writable locations must declare a\n  3815\tcompatible profile or fail with a guest binding error before the body.\n  3816\tSilently allocating a temporary and claiming writeback is forbidden.\n  3817\tA location extension must define read/write operations, alias identity,\n  3818\tevaluation of nested paths exactly once, lifetime, ownership, cleanup,\n  3819\tand suspension. Generic callers must not decode PHP reference markers\n  3820\tor bypass its copy/count rules.\n  3821\t\n  3822\tFunctions passed, returned, or called recursively keep the common entry\n  3823\tand original identity. This includes calls back into a runtime already\n  3824\ton the stack. No caller-side rewrapping or language-pair cache is allowed.\n  3825\t\n  3826\tThese are in-task rules. A closure, continuation, cell, or live invocation\n  3827\tis not made portable by this convention. Linker/UCF custody and admission\n  3828\tstill govern task/host crossings; currently refused cell-bearing lifts\n  3829\tremain refused. Live closures in an invocation must not be placed in\n  3830\tcanonical literal data or sent as a purported portable request.\n  4017\tRequired evidence:\n  4018\t\n  4019\t- **Local semantics:** existing suites preserve argument order, defaults,\n  4020\t  required/extra arguments, keyword errors, receivers, exceptions, and\n  4021\t  supported reference/static behavior.\n  4022\t- **Direct calls:** each implemented frontend calls every other\n  4023\t  conforming frontend through the same mechanism in both directions\n  4024\t  with compatible values. Derive the test matrix from admitted\n  4025\t  frontends; do not hard-code it into runtime dispatch.\n  4026\t- **Higher-order calls:** pass, return, store, recurse, and call back\n  4027\t  through received functions. Assert identity and captures without\n  4028\t  replacement cells.\n  4029\t- **Callable admission:** source data with an entry-spelled property\n  4030\t  remains data; profile-constructed descriptors are admitted. Exercise\n  4031\t  supported PHP string/array designators both under local resolution and\n  4032\t  explicit callable export, preserving required late lookup without\n  4033\t  foreign namespace guessing.\nrg: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.clojure.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: docs/design/yang.clojure.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n     7\t## Core Philosophy\n     8\t\n     9\tEverything is data.\n    10\tInterpretation > abstraction.\n    11\tExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\n    12\tRestrictions are a feature.\n    13\t\n    14\t### Foundational Axioms\n    15\t\n    16\t1. **Everything is a Stream**: Portable I/O and system data flow through append-only streams; hosts may also install explicit local functions that perform direct I/O.\n    17\t2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\n    18\t   At system scale, a \"system\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\n    19\t   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\n    20\t   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\n    21\t3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n    22\t4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\n    23\t\n    24\t## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n    25\t\n    26\t- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n    27\t- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n    28\t- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n    29\t- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n    30\t- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n    31\t- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n    32\t- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\n    48\tStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n    49\t\n    50\tA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\n    51\tof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\n    52\tsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\n    53\tstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\n    54\tthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\n    55\tanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\n    56\texists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\n    57\tthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\n    58\tand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\n    59\tbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\n    60\tthe stream's own.\n   112\t## Code Style\n   113\t\n   114\t- Prefer simple data over rich types.\n   115\t- Prefer total functions over partial ones.\n   116\t- Prefer declarative pipelines over imperative logic.\n   117\t- Avoid cleverness.\n   118\t- Name things after what they do to streams.\n   119\t\n   120\t## Development Workflow\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1,150p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '95,165p;1615,1645p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '215,230p;1028,1057p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '2360,2405p;4220,4285p'; rg -n 'js/callable\\\\?|js/call\\\\b|py/call-kw|php/callable-of|php/call-value' src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.clojure.prelude\n     2\t  \"The `clj` runtime module (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.10):\n     3\t   the published linker module every linked clojure program requires, as\n     4\t   `js`, `php` and `py` are for their frontends. It is written in prelude\n     5\t   notation and emitted with the same core machinery those preludes use;\n     6\t   it never runs on the host.\n     7\t\n     8\t   Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\n     9\t\n    10\t   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\n    11\t     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\n    12\t     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\n    13\t     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\n    14\t     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\n    15\t     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\n    16\t     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\n    17\t     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\n    18\t     standing);\n    19\t   - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\n    20\t     `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\n    21\t     allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\n    22\t     program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\n    23\t     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\n    24\t     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\n    25\t     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\n    26\t     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\n    27\t     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\n    28\t     module dictionary are the same seam;\n    29\t   - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\n    30\t     needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\n    31\t     adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\n    32\t     predicates read.\n    33\t\n    34\t   The module pins the shared calling runtime (`yang.call`) at the\n    35\t   convention's call-address, as the other runtimes do, and refuses before\n    36\t   anything is published when a free name nothing supplies is read.\"\n    37\t  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    38\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n    39\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    40\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    41\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(def module-name\n    45\t  \"The linker module name of the clojure runtime.\"\n    46\t  'clj)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def runtime-keys\n    50\t  \"Every runtime key, each with an `:clj/uninit` placeholder at module\n    51\t   level so every read is discharged before `clj/init!` allocates the\n    52\t   real cell. They stay qualified: internal store keys, never guest\n    53\t   names.\"\n    54\t  '[clj.rt/state clj.rt/globals])\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(def definitions\n    58\t  \"The module's definition list, in prelude notation (the module's own\n    59\t   `clj/` prefix is stripped on emit).\"\n    60\t  '[;; ------------------------------------------------- state and namespace\n    61\t    [clj/init!\n    62\t     (fn []\n    63\t       (if (= clj.rt/state :clj/uninit)\n    64\t         (do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))\n    65\t             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/state) :clj/ready))\n    66\t         :clj/ready))]\n    67\t    ;; the runtime global namespace: one task-local map in a cell, keyed by\n    68\t    ;; export name. `clj/define-global!` answers the value, so a publish\n    69\t    ;; sequence can chain through it.\n    70\t    [clj/define-global!\n    71\t     (fn [name value]\n    72\t       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\n    73\t                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\n    74\t           value))]\n    75\t    [clj/global-get\n    76\t     (fn [name]\n    77\t       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    78\t         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    79\t         :clj/unbound))]\n    80\t\n    81\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- entry\n    82\t    ;; The outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper is frontend-\n    83\t    ;; internal, so the entry removes one wrapper level from the\n    84\t    ;; program's value (a program returning that vector as data was\n    85\t    ;; wrapped again, so one level is exact). An error outcome passes\n    86\t    ;; through as the failure value for the caller to render.\n    87\t    [clj/unwrap-outcome\n    88\t     (fn [value]\n    89\t       (if (if (data/vector? value) (= (data/count value) 2) false)\n    90\t         (if (= (data/nth value 0) :yin.k/ok)\n    91\t           (data/nth value 1)\n    92\t           value)\n    93\t         value))]\n    94\t    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\n    95\t    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\n    96\t    [clj/run-main\n    97\t     (fn [body]\n    98\t       (do (clj/init!)\n    99\t           (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(def module-definitions\n   103\t  \"The module's definition list: an `:clj/uninit` placeholder for every\n   104\t   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n   105\t  (core/module-definitions \"clj\" :clj/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(def module-uast\n   109\t  \"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\n   110\t   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level.\"\n   111\t  (core/module-tree module-definitions []))\n   112\t\n   113\t\n   114\t(def module-exports\n   115\t  \"The module's exports: every `clj/` key of the definition list, stripped.\"\n   116\t  (core/exports \"clj\" definitions))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(def ^:private module-free-names\n   120\t  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the host\n   121\t   exports its manifest must declare.\"\n   122\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(defn module-spec\n   126\t  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `clj` over\n   127\t   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call`\n   128\t   module at `call-address` — the convention's call-address, as every\n   129\t   runtime's publication carries. A free name nothing supplies is refused\n   130\t   before anything is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n   131\t  [registry call-address]\n   132\t  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\n   133\t                     :ast module-uast,\n   134\t                     :exports module-exports,\n   135\t                     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n   136\t                     :free-names module-free-names,\n   137\t                     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n   138\t                     :registry registry,\n   139\t                     :message \"the clj module reads an undeclared name\",\n   140\t                     :refusal-ns \"yang.clojure\"}))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(defn register-library-module\n   144\t  \"Return `registry` with host module `name` installed over `entries`\n   145\t   (`[export function]` pairs) at `arities`, each export pure.\"\n   146\t  [registry name entries arities]\n   147\t  (module/register-host-module\n   148\t    registry name\n   149\t    (into {} entries)\n   150\t    (into {} (map (fn [[op _]] [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\n    95\t           integer/format integer/parse integer/float-digits\n    96\t           integer/decimal->float}\n    97\t        call/host-names))\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t(defquoted ^:private core-definitions\n   101\t  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n   102\t  '[;; ----------------------------------------------------------------- kinds\n   103\t    [js/cell? (fn [x] (= (get x :type) :cell-ref))]\n   104\t    [js/symbol?\n   105\t     (fn [x]\n   106\t       (if (js/cell? x) (= (get (cell/get x) :js/type) :symbol) false))]\n   107\t    [js/object? (fn [x] (if (js/cell? x) (not (js/symbol? x)) false))]\n   108\t    [js/make-symbol\n   109\t     (fn [description]\n   110\t       (cell/new (assoc (assoc {} :js/type :symbol) :description description)))]\n   111\t    [js/str?\n   112\t     (fn [x]\n   113\t       (if (nil? (get x :js/str)) (not (nil? (get x :js/units))) true))]\n   114\t    [js/pair (fn [a b] (conj (conj [] a) b))]\n   115\t    [js/vconj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n   116\t    [js/arg (fn [args i] (get args i :js/undefined))]\n   117\t    [js/kind-of\n   118\t     ;; undefined null boolean number bigint string function object. A\n   119\t     ;; number is float64 content, a bigint a bare exact integer: content\n   120\t     ;; equality with the same value as float64 tells them apart on every\n   121\t     ;; host (the JS carrier is not a host number at all)\n   122\t     (fn [x]\n   123\t       (if (= x :js/undefined)\n   124\t         :undefined\n   125\t         (if (= x :js/null)\n   126\t           :null\n   127\t           (if 