{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"There is already a concrete counterexample in the matrix: TypeScript passes a closure into Clojure’s `(defn clj_apply [f] (+ (f 20) 1))`. The call through `f` has no projected-name position, so the proposed rule would send it to map lookup. Projected exports can also be immutable Clojure descriptors, so a projected name cannot by itself imply `cell/get`.\n"}}
